                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3913b2a2-daca-45a6-8f33-e5d4b4b30ab8",
                        "source_entry_id": "72373f86-d5ed-3c6f-91aa-5edbdda21bc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "c2896d30-e5ab-356f-afee-db86b17732b9",
                        "source_sense_description": "middeleeuws dichter en zanger in Noord-Frankrijk",
                        "target_lang_word": "trouvère",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trouvère",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "373a2ff0-5116-351c-be16-7f0c1b0a611c",
                                        "entry_id": "2519f966-39bf-3106-ab16-6d3fe95672fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A medieval lyric poet using the Northern langue d’oïl (precursor dialects of modern French), as opposed to their older, southern example, the original troubadours, who used langue d’oc (Occitan)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afbc0ba7-11a0-43de-bead-3c08d239044e",
                                                "sense_id": "373a2ff0-5116-351c-be16-7f0c1b0a611c",
                                                "text": "The activities of Jewish singers immediately before the expulsion from Spain testifies that they were outsiders in every respect, regarded neither as Jews nor Christians. They also appeared in the company of troubadours and trouvers, and like Suesskind of Trimberg (c.1220); these Jewish singers mastered the international repertoire no less than their Gentile colleagues."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d1706d0-d546-41d7-a163-1a88a4c74145",
                        "source_entry_id": "72373f86-d5ed-3c6f-91aa-5edbdda21bc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "c2896d30-e5ab-356f-afee-db86b17732b9",
                        "source_sense_description": "middeleeuws dichter en zanger in Noord-Frankrijk",
                        "target_lang_word": "trouveur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trouveur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ccaf800c-45a0-3f79-a062-54f4745791c8",
                                        "entry_id": "716819e4-4b3b-3c2f-a078-807c1f6a9a48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A minstrel, a troubadour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9c68e39-639f-46e2-8045-994be2005e51",
                                                "sense_id": "ccaf800c-45a0-3f79-a062-54f4745791c8",
                                                "text": "1796, Robert Southey, Joan of Arc, Book IV, 1829, The Poetical Works of Robert Southey, page 16,\nMeantime the Trouveur struck the harp; he sang\nOf Lancelot du Lake, the truest Knight\nThat ever loved fair Lady;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a97406ad-09fa-4e9a-9dce-74564daa4c89",
                                                "sense_id": "ccaf800c-45a0-3f79-a062-54f4745791c8",
                                                "text": "But, secondly, a great many of these tales were borrowed from the narratives of the trouveurs or minstrels who wandered through the north of France, relating stories or reciting poems for the amusement of their entertainers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77986f86-d50b-4b94-bf5b-0235b4fce7e6",
                                                "sense_id": "ccaf800c-45a0-3f79-a062-54f4745791c8",
                                                "text": "The origin of these tales must be traced to the inventions of the Trouveurs, who doubtless often adopted them from various nations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a53067c3-ee0a-4ae3-a419-0721f51e228c",
                        "source_entry_id": "72373f86-d5ed-3c6f-91aa-5edbdda21bc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "c2896d30-e5ab-356f-afee-db86b17732b9",
                        "source_sense_description": "middeleeuws dichter en zanger in Noord-Frankrijk",
                        "target_lang_word": "trouvère",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trouvère",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c54e288-6377-39cd-81ae-56f0fb6da4c3",
                                        "entry_id": "21ff9af0-09d4-3eb1-80a5-ccf8eb48f3cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ancien poète lyrique de cour qui composait et chantait en langue d’oïl en s’accompagnant d’un instrument dans le nord de la France du XIIᵉ au XIVᵉ siècles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f562cb61-54dd-4708-a12f-0e7d67dd7557",
                                                "sense_id": "2c54e288-6377-39cd-81ae-56f0fb6da4c3",
                                                "text": "Ainsi, la poésie lyrique des troubadours et des trouvères, et surtout la portion de cette poésie qui roule sur les sentimens de galanterie chevaleresque, n’a pas une source latine ; cette poésie est née avec la galanterie chevaleresque elle-même, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01885944-a792-4820-afe3-878a3f58d7a4",
                                                "sense_id": "2c54e288-6377-39cd-81ae-56f0fb6da4c3",
                                                "text": "Dois-je faire état du témoignage imprécis des trouvères, du rapport si peu positif de Wace, des affirmations empressées de nos archéologues-poètes ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44af64b7-78e2-4342-bc75-e46b54451a4a",
                                                "sense_id": "2c54e288-6377-39cd-81ae-56f0fb6da4c3",
                                                "text": "Quelquefois aussi le trouvère chantait et viélait tout à la fois, les citations abondent qui nous montrent tour à tour les musiciens sous ces deux aspects."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9a0f051-86a0-3951-9136-a20348b24cb7",
                                        "entry_id": "21ff9af0-09d4-3eb1-80a5-ccf8eb48f3cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Auteur-compositeur-interprète des époques ultérieures, ou simplement poète ou écrivain, rappelant par son style ou ses thèmes de prédilection les trouvères médiévaux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e53189-b609-43ea-8b27-b7a4d14f9a27",
                                                "sense_id": "d9a0f051-86a0-3951-9136-a20348b24cb7",
                                                "text": "Et qui mieux que ce trouvère d’aujourd’hui pour chanter la folie de ces deux amants éternels ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
